From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add an offline security check to browser and desktop

Port the useful parts of NodeWarden's security dashboard to the clients
without adding a server-side dependency. The page reads the unlocked vault
locally, flags weak and reused passwords, asks Have I Been Pwned with the
standard SHA-1 k-anonymity prefix, and lists logins that have no TOTP saved.

The HIBP request never sends a password or a full hash. The page only creates a
five-character prefix, so it continues to work with the same privacy model as
the upstream breach report. The check is available in both the browser popup
and the Electron desktop window.
